  "memo": "Advanced Micro Devices (AMD) has demonstrated robust momentum across its recent fiscal years, driven by accelerated server and accelerator revenue growth. In its most recently completed fiscal year, FY2025 (ending January 31, 2025), AMD reported revenue of $26.09 billion, marking significant double-digit growth over the prior year's $23.12 billion. The company achieved a non-GAAP net income of $3.71 billion and a non-GAAP earnings per share of $3.51, alongside a non-GAAP operating margin of 23%. GAAP net income rose to $2.38 billion, and free cash flow reached $3.5 billion. Looking back at FY2024 (ending January 31, 2024), revenue was $23.12 billion with non-GAAP EPS of $1.71. Further back, FY2023 revenue totaled $19.75 billion, with non-GAAP EPS of $1.39. This trajectory underscores AMD's strategic pivot toward AI and high-performance computing, scaling its financial performance rapidly as demand for its MI300 and EPYC processors surges. AMD’s accelerating profitability and expanding market share position it as a compelling long-term value play amid the global AI hardware supercycle."
